arguments.prompt:
You are building a Blazor Web App (.NET 11, static SSR, no interactivity) for a university course catalog. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-be68fb14dfc64804af0517c0fde1e685/UniversityCourseCatalog`.

## Requirements
1. **Homepage** – featured courses, department links
2. **Course catalog page** – searchable, filterable list of courses (filter by department, search by name/code)
3. **Course detail page** – description, schedule, credits, instructor bio
4. **Enrollment request form** – name, student ID, course selection dropdown, submit; standard HTML form with POST, confirmation message on success
5. **No authentication**
6. Intranet deployment (fast connectivity), static SSR only

## Architecture
- **Models** in `Models/` folder: `Department`, `Course`, `Instructor`, `EnrollmentRequest`
- **Services** in `Services/` folder: `ICatalogService` / `CatalogService` with in-memory seed data (at least 4 departments, 12+ courses, varied instructors)
- **Pages**: Home, Catalog (with query string filters), CourseDetail (route param), Enroll, EnrollmentConfirmation

## Existing project structure
```
UniversityCourseCatalog/
  Components/
    App.razor
    Layout/
      MainLayout.razor, MainLayout.razor.css, NavMenu.razor, NavMenu.razor.css, NavMenu.razor.js
    Pages/
      Home.razor, Weather.razor, Error.razor, NotFound.razor
    Routes.razor
    _Imports.razor
  Program.cs
  wwwroot/
    app.css
```

## What to do

### 1. Create Models
Create `Models/Department.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Department
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Create `Models/Instructor.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Instructor
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Bio { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Email { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Create `Models/Course.cs`:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class Course
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Code { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int Credits { get; set; }
    public string Schedule { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Location { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public int MaxEnrollment { get; set; }
    public bool IsFeatured { get; set; }
    public int DepartmentId { get; set; }
    public Department Department { get; set; } = null!;
    public int InstructorId { get; set; }
    public Instructor Instructor { get; set; } = null!;
}
```

Create `Models/EnrollmentRequest.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public class EnrollmentRequest
{
    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Name is required.")]
    [StringLength(100)]
    public string StudentName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Student ID is required.")]
    [RegularExpression(@"^[A-Z]{2}\d{6}$", ErrorMessage = "Student ID must be in format XX000000 (2 letters followed by 6 digits).")]
    public string StudentId { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    [Range(1, int.MaxValue, ErrorMessage = "Please select a course.")]
    public int CourseId { get; set; }

    public string? Comments { get; set; }
}
```

### 2. Create Service
Create `Services/ICatalogService.cs` and `Services/CatalogService.cs`.

The interface:
```csharp
namespace UniversityCourseCatalog.Services;

using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models;

public interface ICatalogService
{
    IReadOnlyList<Department> GetDepartments();
    Department? GetDepartment(int id);
    IReadOnlyList<Course> GetCourses(string? searchTerm = null, int? departmentId = null);
    IReadOnlyList<Course> GetFeaturedCourses();
    Course? GetCourse(int id);
    IReadOnlyList<Course> GetCoursesByDepartment(int departmentId);
    void SubmitEnrollmentRequest(EnrollmentRequest request);
}
```

The implementation should have rich seed data with at least:
- 4 departments: Computer Science (CS), Mathematics (MATH), Physics (PHYS), English (ENGL)
- 8+ instructors with realistic bios
- 12+ courses spread across departments, some marked as featured
- Courses with realistic schedules like "MWF 9:00–9:50 AM", "TR 1:00–2:15 PM"

For `GetCourses`, filter by search term (matching course name or code, case-insensitive) and/or departmentId. `SubmitEnrollmentRequest` just stores in an in-memory list (no persistence needed).

### 3. Update Program.cs
Register the service:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<ICatalogService, CatalogService>();
```
Add the using for Services namespace.

### 4. Update NavMenu.razor
Replace the nav links with: Home, Courses, Enroll. Remove Weather link. Update the brand to "University Course Catalog".

### 5. Delete Weather.razor
Remove `Components/Pages/Weather.razor`.

### 6. Create/Update Pages

**Home.razor** – Replace existing content:
- Page title "University Course Catalog"
- Welcome banner/hero section
- "Featured Courses" section showing featured courses as Bootstrap cards (course name, code, credits, department, link to detail)
- "Departments" section showing department cards with links to the catalog filtered by department

**Catalog.razor** at route `/courses`:
- Accept `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` for `Search` (string) and `DepartmentId` (int?)
- Show search input and department dropdown filter in a form (GET method to self)
- Display matching courses in a responsive table or card list: Code, Name, Department, Credits, Schedule, link to detail page
- Show a "no results" message if nothing matches

**CourseDetail.razor** at route `/courses/{Id:int}`:
- Inject ICatalogService, look up course by Id
- If not found, show "Course not found" message
- Otherwise display: course name, code, department link, description, credits, schedule, location, max enrollment
- Instructor section: name, title, email, bio
- "Enroll in this course" link to the enrollment page

**Enroll.razor** at route `/enroll`:
- Standard HTML form with POST to itself using EditForm with FormName
- Fields: Student Name (text), Student ID (text with placeholder "e.g. AB123456"), Course (dropdown from service), Comments (textarea, optional)
- Show validation messages
- On valid submit, call service.SubmitEnrollmentRequest and redirect to `/enroll/confirmation`
- Accept optional `[SupplyParameterFromQuery]` CourseId to pre-select the dropdown

**EnrollmentConfirmation.razor** at route `/enroll/confirmation`:
- Simple confirmation page: "Your enrollment request has been submitted successfully."
- Links back to course catalog and home

### 7. Update _Imports.razor
Add:
```
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Models
@using UniversityCourseCatalog.Services
```

### 8. Update App.razor title
Change the `<title>` if present to "University Course Catalog".

### 9. Update MainLayout.razor
Update the top-row link from "About" to something like the university name or remove it. Keep it clean.

### 10. Add custom CSS
Append to `wwwroot/app.css` some simple styles for the catalog:
- A hero/banner section style
- Card hover effects
- Any spacing/typography tweaks

### 11. Build and verify
Run `dotnet build` to ensure it compiles without errors.

IMPORTANT: 
- Use the `edit` tool for existing files, `create` tool for new files.
- Make sure all pages use `@page` directive with correct routes.
- Use `@inject ICatalogService CatalogService` in pages that need data.
- For the enrollment form, use Blazor's `EditForm` with `Model` binding and `FormName` for static SSR form handling.
- For navigation after form submit, use `NavigationManager.NavigateTo("/enroll/confirmation")`.
- The enrollment form page needs `@rendermode` left as default (static SSR) and use `[SupplyParameterFromForm]` for the model.

